From: PB624 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: pcf8563: take the IRQ trigger type from firmware

On the PocketBook 624 the PCF8563 INT shares the A13 NMI line with the
AXP209, whose driver requests it without a trigger type.  The hardcoded
IRQF_TRIGGER_LOW makes the shared request fail with -EBUSY (flags
mismatch); the line is level-low anyway.

---
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c	2026-10-10 18:41:29.576239950 +0300
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c	2026-10-10 18:41:29.580240083 +0300
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@
 	if (client->irq > 0) {
 		err = devm_request_threaded_irq(&client->dev, client->irq,
 				NULL, pcf8563_irq,
-				IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_TRIGGER_LOW,
+				IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT,
 				pcf8563_driver.driver.name, client);
 		if (err) {
 			dev_err(&client->dev, "unable to request IRQ %d\n",
